# Release signing config for Retro-Saturn.
#
# Copy this file to `key.properties` (same directory) and fill in the real
# values. `key.properties` is gitignored; the example is checked in so the
# schema survives across checkouts.
#
# These four values are the same set the legacy ymir-android Play Store
# listing was signed with. The keystore itself is registered with Play
# Console under `com.crownpark.ymir_multiplatform` -- keeping the signing
# key means Retro-Saturn ships as an update of the existing listing, not a
# brand-new app, so existing users receive it automatically and reviews /
# install counts carry over. See `android/app/build.gradle.kts` for how
# the values are consumed.
#
# When `key.properties` is absent (the default on a fresh checkout), the
# release build falls back to the debug keystore and prints a warning -- so
# `flutter run --release` still works in dev. Real release builds for the
# Play Store require this file.
storeFile=/absolute/path/to/your-upload-keystore.jks
storePassword=your-keystore-password
keyAlias=your-key-alias
keyPassword=your-key-password